// CoderOS screen recording: the microphone's supervisor (docs/os/2026-10-30-coderos-and-coax-audit.md,
// step 2 row 4), in place of screen-record's supervise_audio, watch_capture, end_capture,
// resolve_audio_target, node_present, write_mic_report and mark_mic_outage (openagents 2ca255550e).
// screen-record starts it beside the picture and it runs until the take's stop file appears:
//   coax/web/tool.sh os/record-audio.coax supervise OUTPUT T0 TARGET PICK [--system] [--name NODE]
// OUTPUT is the take's video path, T0 its start (epoch seconds, as `date +%s.%N` wrote it), TARGET
// the node to read first (an id, or a name) and PICK the microphone report it was chosen with
// (os/microphone.coax's JSON; "" when there is none). --system reads the default sink's monitor
// instead of a microphone; --name is the node name the take asked for.
// What it does, as the shell did, and why (each from a take that lost sound):
//   - each capture is a segment, OUTPUT.audio.wav then OUTPUT.audio.001.wav..., and the ledger
//     META.audio.segments gets `index<TAB>offset<TAB>path` as it opens, the offset on the take's
//     clock, so a hole keeps the sound after it in place (2026-09-09);
//   - a capture is watched, not only waited on: one whose file stops growing for OUTAGE_MIN, or
//     whose node goes away while pw-record lives, is ended there (2026-09-11), and each growth is
//     logged in the segment's .clock file for the microphone-clock fit;
//   - while the microphone is gone it is looked for again by name, at 1, 2 then 3 seconds, the
//     take is told once (and again after OUTAGE_LIMIT), META.audio.outage holds where the sound
//     stopped, and META.mic says live false so the HUD shows it.
// The files, their formats and the messages are the shell's, so screen-record's stop and the HUD
// read a take made by either. Timings come from CODEROS_RECORD_AUDIO_{POLL,DEVICE_POLL,OUTAGE_MIN,
// OUTAGE_LIMIT} as they did.
#import "Basic";
#load "../coax/lib/sys/tool.coax";
#load "../coax/lib/sys/fs.coax";
#load "../coax/lib/sys/args.coax";
#load "../coax/lib/sys/proc.coax";
#load "../coax/lib/json/json.coax";
#load "../coax/lib/text/regex.coax";
#load "mic-pick.coax";
#load "record-policy.coax";

#load "record-supervise.coax";

tool_main :: () -> int #export_c {
  a: [1] Args;
  if !args_load(a[..]) { return 2; }
  return ra_main(a[..]);
}
